From: Jonas Meyer-Ohle <19151471+jonas-meyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: uvc: treat -ENODATA as a missed isochronous
 transfer

dwc2 completes an isochronous request whose target microframe has passed
with -ENODATA. dwc3 uses -EXDEV for the same case. uvc_video_complete()
handles only -EXDEV as a missed transfer. Any other status cancels the
whole queue with uvcg_queue_cancel().

On dwc2, a single late interrupt then cuts the frame on the bus without
UVC_STREAM_ERR, and the host shows a torn frame. The following buffers
are returned with an error too. With -EXDEV handling, the remaining
packets of the frame carry UVC_STREAM_ERR, and the host drops only that
frame.

Handle -ENODATA like -EXDEV.

---
--- a/uvc_video.c
+++ b/uvc_video.c
@@ -359,6 +359,7 @@
 		break;
 
 	case -EXDEV:
+	case -ENODATA:	/* dwc2: the target microframe has passed. */
 		uvcg_dbg(&video->uvc->func, "VS request missed xfer.\n");
 		if (req->length != 0)
 			queue->flags |= UVC_QUEUE_DROP_INCOMPLETE;
